  "spatialDefinition": "WUP 2025 DEGURBA urban centres: contiguous high-density areas, at least 1,500 residents/km² and 50,000 residents. These are not necessarily municipalities or functional metropolitan areas; entries can be suburbs or named urban clusters. Preserve country, cityCode and coordinates when researching them.",
  "qualityNotes": [
    "Pop_plausibility is copied as a literal string from the official bulk CSV for 2025, joined by LocID and City_Code. Catalog documentation relates this field to the time lag and resolution of the input census grids.",
    "The methodological report describes a 0–3 plausibility assessment using comparison datasets, while the bulk CSV contains Low, Moderate and High strings. Their relationship is unresolved; this queue does not claim to reproduce the report’s 11,743-city screened cohort.",
    "The bulk CSV gives 10,551 Moderate/High cities with 2025 population. Of these, 9,407 have a usable 2015 baseline. The filter assesses the 2025 estimate, not the reliability of the entire growth trajectory.",
    "Historical values are estimates. Large percentage changes can reflect settlement expansion, population redistribution or estimation changes; validate extreme trajectories locally before using them as planning evidence.",
    "Missing historical population is excluded, never treated as zero. The ten-year average does not imply the same rate in 2020–2025 or future years.",
    "2025–2035 projection comparisons below are a separate forecast. They use the same eligible cohort restricted to positive 2035 values, not an exhaustive ranking of new cities without a 2015 baseline. Missing projections are excluded, never treated as zero.",
    "countryHasIntegratedCity only means an app city exists in the same country. It does not mean a parcel source covers the candidate. Existing city markers may also cover only part of a city."
  ],
